1
00:00:02,002 --> 00:00:03,630
<i>Previously on</i> Gotham...

2
00:00:03,804 --> 00:00:05,033
You left me the virus.

3
00:00:05,205 --> 00:00:06,400
You've got two options.

4
00:00:06,573 --> 00:00:08,007
<i>You can take the virus.</i>

5
00:00:08,175 --> 00:00:09,855
And find the strength
and get out of there.

6
00:00:10,444 --> 00:00:13,608
<i>Or you can make that
coffin your permanent home.</i>

7
00:00:21,321 --> 00:00:23,449
Fish! Why are you here?

8
00:00:23,657 --> 00:00:24,681
I was alive.

9
00:00:25,025 --> 00:00:26,323
Goodbye, Fish!

10
00:00:30,531 --> 00:00:31,760
Then I was dead.

11
00:00:32,165 --> 00:00:34,361
Let's try subject 13, shall we?

12
00:00:38,539 --> 00:00:39,905
<i>And then I was alive.</i>

13
00:00:43,544 --> 00:00:44,568
<i>Impossible.</i>

14
00:00:44,778 --> 00:00:48,306
Nothing is impossible.

15
00:00:52,553 --> 00:00:54,215
Things are looking up.

16
00:00:54,755 --> 00:00:56,485
My little Penguin and I...

17
00:00:56,757 --> 00:00:58,123
Will be leaving.

18
00:00:59,192 --> 00:01:02,651
This detonator will
trigger the bomb.

19
00:01:02,829 --> 00:01:05,355
Thousands will be
infected with a virus.

20
00:01:05,566 --> 00:01:08,502
Let Gotham fall so you may rise.

21
00:01:08,735 --> 00:01:10,499
I won't have him turn
you into a murderer.

22
00:01:10,804 --> 00:01:12,670
No, you will press it.

23
00:01:15,242 --> 00:01:17,074
When you're ready,
come and find me.

24
00:01:31,825 --> 00:01:32,986
Oh, my.

25
00:01:33,393 --> 00:01:35,473
What is that? WOMAN:
What's happening out there?

26
00:01:37,030 --> 00:01:39,226
My money, my
savings. My savings...

27
00:01:39,399 --> 00:01:40,560
Excuse me, what?

28
00:01:40,734 --> 00:01:43,932
My money, my savings. I want them.
My money, my savings. My whole life.

29
00:01:44,104 --> 00:01:46,733
What's your account number?

30
00:01:46,907 --> 00:01:48,773
My money, my savings...

31
00:01:49,509 --> 00:01:52,274
My money, my savings.
My money, my savings.

32
00:01:52,546 --> 00:01:55,141
Uh, this account was
closed due to unpaid fees.

33
00:01:55,315 --> 00:01:57,795
No, no, my money, my savings,
my life, everything! I have to...

34
00:01:57,884 --> 00:02:00,444
You have no money,
the account is closed.

35
00:02:01,755 --> 00:02:04,020
Give me my money, now!

36
00:02:04,191 --> 00:02:06,490
Oh, God. Um, security!

37
00:02:06,893 --> 00:02:09,226
Hey! What are you...

38
00:02:11,898 --> 00:02:15,562
My money! My savings! Now!

39
00:02:23,110 --> 00:02:24,237
Get out!

40
00:02:24,544 --> 00:02:26,069
- Hey, man! Hey!
- Stop this!

41
00:02:26,246 --> 00:02:29,512
Come here! Come
back! Buy our cookies!

42
00:02:46,800 --> 00:02:48,860
Move on!

43
00:03:08,922 --> 00:03:09,946
<i>Killer.</i>

44
00:03:11,391 --> 00:03:12,586
<i>Killer.</i>

45
00:03:13,827 --> 00:03:14,988
<i>You're a killer.</i>

46
00:03:17,431 --> 00:03:18,592
<i>Killer.</i>

47
00:03:20,100 --> 00:03:21,227
<i>Killer.</i>

48
00:03:21,768 --> 00:03:22,861
<i>Killer!</i>

49
00:03:24,171 --> 00:03:25,833
- Jim?
- Yeah.

50
00:03:26,440 --> 00:03:27,533
You okay?

51
00:03:28,742 --> 00:03:29,869
Fine.

52
00:03:36,216 --> 00:03:37,775
I'm fine, Harvey.

53
00:03:38,051 --> 00:03:42,250
Listen, I hate to do this to you, pal.
But I'm gonna have to ask for your gun.

54
00:03:42,989 --> 00:03:46,790
This virus is tearing the city apart.
You need me. I can control this.

55
00:03:46,993 --> 00:03:49,121
That's why I'm not
asking for your badge.

56
00:03:49,663 --> 00:03:51,529
Some of the guys are talking.

57
00:03:51,832 --> 00:03:55,496
These cops are gonna be watching
you for the smallest sign. Okay?

58
00:03:55,669 --> 00:03:58,002
And if you've got a gun,
they'll be double jumpy.

59
00:03:58,171 --> 00:04:00,072
It's for your own protection.

60
00:04:07,447 --> 00:04:08,540
Any word on Lee?

61
00:04:09,449 --> 00:04:11,441
<i>Nada.</i> What happened
after the bombing?

62
00:04:11,718 --> 00:04:15,177
A mob of infected swarmed the clock
tower. She disappeared in the chaos.

63
00:04:15,355 --> 00:04:17,200
I don't get it. She went
through all that effort

64
00:04:17,224 --> 00:04:19,591
to get you infected with
the virus, then she just bolts?

65
00:04:19,760 --> 00:04:24,494
She saw I was fighting it. She's
waiting for me to give over to it.

66
00:04:26,733 --> 00:04:28,326
Prove her wrong.

67
00:04:32,572 --> 00:04:34,006
Where's Bruce?

68
00:04:48,388 --> 00:04:49,720
Detective Gordon.

69
00:04:51,024 --> 00:04:54,222
Alfred. Has he said anything?

70
00:04:54,528 --> 00:04:56,463
No, no, he just
sits there staring.

71
00:04:58,165 --> 00:04:59,929
I need to talk to him, Harvey.

72
00:05:00,133 --> 00:05:01,658
We're sure that's not the clone?

73
00:05:01,835 --> 00:05:02,996
No, that's Bruce.

74
00:05:03,170 --> 00:05:06,402
God knows what those bastards done
to him, but he's utterly brainwashed.

75
00:05:06,573 --> 00:05:08,565
Are you really the best
person to talk to him?

76
00:05:08,742 --> 00:05:10,953
<i>I mean, from what you said,
you killed his mentor or something.</i>

77
00:05:10,977 --> 00:05:12,070
<i>He might be a bit peeved.</i>

78
00:05:12,245 --> 00:05:16,649
Listen, whatever they did to
him, that is Bruce Wayne in there.

79
00:05:16,917 --> 00:05:19,716
That boy is stronger than
you can possibly imagine.

80
00:05:20,153 --> 00:05:24,284
I just need to make
him remember who he is.

81
00:05:25,125 --> 00:05:26,855
As long as he doesn't
leave the precinct.

82
00:05:27,794 --> 00:05:29,558
Harvey, something
you need to see.

83
00:05:38,471 --> 00:05:40,963
An antidote? Lucius,
I could kiss your face.

84
00:05:41,141 --> 00:05:43,252
Before you do that. I don't
actually have the formula.

85
00:05:43,276 --> 00:05:44,954
But there is an antidote.
That's what you're saying?

86
00:05:44,978 --> 00:05:47,590
I was going through the papers you
recovered from the Owl leader's house.

87
00:05:47,614 --> 00:05:50,516
They suggest that while Strange was
working to weaponize the Tetch virus,

88
00:05:50,684 --> 00:05:52,653
he was also working
on a parallel project,

89
00:05:52,819 --> 00:05:55,550
tailoring different antiviral
agents to his own ends.

90
00:05:55,722 --> 00:05:57,623
Strange was
designing an antidote.

91
00:05:57,824 --> 00:05:59,292
That makes sense.

92
00:05:59,526 --> 00:06:03,258
The Court was careful to protect its
own. They would've wanted a safeguard.

93
00:06:03,430 --> 00:06:06,730
We need to talk to Strange. Is he
still here, or has he been moved?

94
00:06:06,967 --> 00:06:09,459
Uh, well, when you
were buried in the coffin

95
00:06:09,636 --> 00:06:11,366
and the city was about
to be virus-bombed,

96
00:06:11,538 --> 00:06:12,801
some decisions had to be made.

97
00:06:13,006 --> 00:06:14,030
Harvey!

98
00:06:14,975 --> 00:06:16,910
I told Alfred to
question Strange.

99
00:06:17,077 --> 00:06:20,343
<i>In exchange for him telling us where
the bombing was gonna go down,</i>

100
00:06:20,513 --> 00:06:24,245
Alfred let Strange walk. Yes,
I'm blaming it on the butler!

101
00:06:26,720 --> 00:06:29,315
All right. Strange is a weasel.

102
00:06:29,723 --> 00:06:32,352
He'd try to get as far
away from this as possible.

103
00:06:32,525 --> 00:06:36,053
Union Station is shut down.
Downtown train station's our best bet.

104
00:06:36,263 --> 00:06:37,788
Yeah. Wait up!

105
00:06:38,265 --> 00:06:39,289
Harvey?

106
00:06:39,466 --> 00:06:42,903
Lucius, I know what you're gonna
say. All right? He can handle this.

107
00:06:43,069 --> 00:06:45,766
Hell, Barnes had the virus
for weeks before anyone knew.

108
00:06:46,139 --> 00:06:48,734
What I was gonna
say, from all I see here,

109
00:06:48,909 --> 00:06:51,845
Strange's virus is an accelerated
version of the Tetch virus.

110
00:06:52,212 --> 00:06:54,477
Why do you think people
are reacting so quickly?

111
00:06:54,648 --> 00:06:56,728
Gordon isn't going to be
able to fight this for long.

112
00:06:57,017 --> 00:06:59,418
Well. We'll just have
to wait and see, huh?

113
00:06:59,586 --> 00:07:01,418
You keep working
on that antidote.

114
00:07:04,457 --> 00:07:06,983
One second, one second!
One ticket at a time.

115
00:07:15,568 --> 00:07:17,161
Sir, excuse me!

116
00:07:23,076 --> 00:07:24,203
Oh!

117
00:07:24,744 --> 00:07:26,212
Excuse me!

118
00:07:27,380 --> 00:07:29,110
Oh, no.

119
00:07:30,583 --> 00:07:34,145
I think you mean,
"Hello, Fish. I miss you."

120
00:07:35,155 --> 00:07:39,422
And don't worry, sweetheart.
The fun has just begun.

121
00:07:50,403 --> 00:07:53,202
<i>As the flames of hedonism</i>

122
00:07:53,940 --> 00:07:58,105
licked the very
foundation of its society,

123
00:07:59,779 --> 00:08:01,839
Nero played and sang

124
00:08:02,015 --> 00:08:05,645
at the destruction of Troy.

125
00:08:08,455 --> 00:08:11,152
I will say this about
the Court of Owls,

126
00:08:11,491 --> 00:08:14,552
they have style.

127
00:08:15,895 --> 00:08:19,161
Not to mention, they've handed
us the perfect opportunity.

128
00:08:19,599 --> 00:08:20,658
For what?

129
00:08:20,834 --> 00:08:22,894
The city is in total disarray.

130
00:08:23,336 --> 00:08:25,771
What better time to
consolidate power?

131
00:08:26,773 --> 00:08:27,900
Barbara?

132
00:08:29,009 --> 00:08:33,379
I have told you, again and again, I
have no interest in running Gotham,

133
00:08:33,680 --> 00:08:36,878
- I only want...
- To kill Penguin. Yes.

134
00:08:37,150 --> 00:08:38,709
I got it the first
billion times.

135
00:08:38,918 --> 00:08:42,685
And where is he now? Oh,
that's right, with Fish Mooney.

136
00:08:42,856 --> 00:08:45,052
- So we find her.
- And then what?

137
00:08:45,225 --> 00:08:49,060
You blast through her army of
goons until you get to Oswald?

138
00:08:49,229 --> 00:08:50,959
You're gonna need muscle, honey.

139
00:08:51,131 --> 00:08:52,861
- Which you provide.
- Oh.

140
00:08:53,366 --> 00:08:55,426
So you expect my help.

141
00:08:56,036 --> 00:08:57,868
But when I need yours

142
00:08:58,238 --> 00:09:02,505
to take advantage of an
opportunity of a lifetime,

143
00:09:03,510 --> 00:09:04,739
nothing.

144
00:09:08,948 --> 00:09:10,041
Baby,

145
00:09:11,718 --> 00:09:13,778
listen, all I ask

146
00:09:13,953 --> 00:09:15,751
is that you use

147
00:09:16,322 --> 00:09:19,850
this beautiful
big brain of yours

148
00:09:20,160 --> 00:09:22,322
to help me finally

149
00:09:23,696 --> 00:09:26,564
get this city under my thumb,

150
00:09:27,267 --> 00:09:30,169
and afterwards, I will help you

151
00:09:30,837 --> 00:09:32,999
pry Penguin away from Fish.

152
00:09:34,741 --> 00:09:35,868
Deal?

153
00:09:37,610 --> 00:09:40,205
I will give you a day.

154
00:09:45,752 --> 00:09:47,311
I thought we were friends.

155
00:09:47,554 --> 00:09:51,252
When the Court of Owls
calls, one does not refuse.

156
00:09:51,691 --> 00:09:53,853
Still, I'm not upset.

157
00:09:54,627 --> 00:09:59,463
I knew when your old masters summoned
you it was to cook up some horror.

158
00:09:59,632 --> 00:10:03,160
And here's the
thing. I need horror.

159
00:10:03,870 --> 00:10:05,790
They're responsible
for all of this, aren't they?

160
00:10:06,072 --> 00:10:07,540
At the behest of The Court,

161
00:10:07,707 --> 00:10:11,439
I weaponized a virus that
releases a person's darkest urges.

162
00:10:12,245 --> 00:10:13,804
Thousands have been infected.

163
00:10:15,348 --> 00:10:17,249
So where is this virus?

164
00:10:18,118 --> 00:10:20,053
I know there's more.

165
00:10:20,220 --> 00:10:22,655
It has all been used.
Please, I must go!

166
00:10:22,822 --> 00:10:26,725
Don't. You will
give me the virus.

167
00:10:26,926 --> 00:10:31,330
You will make me the
army you promised.

168
00:10:31,664 --> 00:10:35,465
You will do everything I say

169
00:10:35,802 --> 00:10:40,001
until this city is in
the palm of my hand.

170
00:10:41,141 --> 00:10:42,632
Are we clear?

171
00:10:43,476 --> 00:10:44,876
Yes, madam.

172
00:10:53,486 --> 00:10:55,250
Sorry, folks, this
exit's off... Ah!

173
00:11:04,731 --> 00:11:08,031
I'll look around for the station
cops, see if they found Strange.

174
00:11:10,069 --> 00:11:11,230
Hello?

175
00:11:12,272 --> 00:11:13,331
Oh, jeez.

176
00:11:13,673 --> 00:11:15,198
He's right here.

177
00:11:19,379 --> 00:11:20,438
This is Gordon.

178
00:11:20,647 --> 00:11:23,412
<i>Hi, Jim. I was just checking in.</i>

179
00:11:23,583 --> 00:11:24,881
<i>Seeing how you're feeling.</i>

180
00:11:25,885 --> 00:11:27,376
<i>Crazy day, huh?</i>

181
00:11:27,787 --> 00:11:30,723
- Lee, where are you?
<i>- Somewhere very familiar to you.</i>

182
00:11:31,324 --> 00:11:32,986
I know how you're feeling.

183
00:11:33,693 --> 00:11:38,961
All that blood rushing through your veins,
your heart beating faster and faster.

184
00:11:42,068 --> 00:11:43,092
Listen to me.

185
00:11:43,269 --> 00:11:45,033
<i>You need to turn
yourself in. It's not safe.</i>

186
00:11:45,238 --> 00:11:47,434
<i>The infected are being
killed all over the city.</i>

187
00:11:47,607 --> 00:11:49,166
Wow, you're really
fighting this, huh?

188
00:11:49,842 --> 00:11:51,674
<i>You know, you don't have to.</i>

189
00:11:51,945 --> 00:11:55,507
<i>The cage is finally
open, Jim. You're free.</i>

190
00:11:56,349 --> 00:11:58,113
- No.
<i>- I thought you loved me.</i>

191
00:11:59,385 --> 00:12:00,945
I thought you wanted
us to be together.

192
00:12:01,054 --> 00:12:02,352
Not like this.

193
00:12:03,423 --> 00:12:07,053
Well, this is the only way, Jim.

194
00:12:07,760 --> 00:12:09,353
<i>Just listen to the whispers.</i>

195
00:12:09,529 --> 00:12:12,363
<i>Killer. Killer.</i>

196
00:12:14,234 --> 00:12:18,103
They'll lead you to me.
Tell you who you are.

197
00:12:18,338 --> 00:12:19,431
<i>Killer.</i>

198
00:12:20,206 --> 00:12:21,674
That's not who I am.

199
00:12:21,841 --> 00:12:23,833
<i>I wonder what they're saying.</i>

200
00:12:24,177 --> 00:12:27,306
<i>That you like hurting
people? Killing people?</i>

201
00:12:27,480 --> 00:12:28,480
<i>Killer.</i>

202
00:12:29,082 --> 00:12:30,948
See how well I know you, Jim?

203
00:12:31,818 --> 00:12:33,912
<i>Now I'm gonna go have some fun.</i>

204
00:12:34,120 --> 00:12:35,816
We'll catch up soon.

205
00:12:36,456 --> 00:12:37,719
Promise.

206
00:12:41,961 --> 00:12:44,362
<i>Killer. Killer.</i>

207
00:12:45,365 --> 00:12:46,993
<i>You're a killer.</i>

208
00:12:48,801 --> 00:12:50,565
Jim? Jim.

209
00:12:51,204 --> 00:12:53,196
Someone spotted Strange.

210
00:12:54,741 --> 00:12:59,145
Just don't shoot any innocent
bystanders. Or me. Especially me.

211
00:13:05,451 --> 00:13:06,680
GCPD!

212
00:13:06,886 --> 00:13:09,355
Don't move! Fish?

213
00:13:11,190 --> 00:13:12,590
What a surprise.

214
00:13:12,759 --> 00:13:15,456
My goodness,
Harvey. You look awful.

215
00:13:15,762 --> 00:13:17,162
It's good to see you, too.

216
00:13:17,397 --> 00:13:19,559
We just want Strange.
You can walk away.

217
00:13:19,766 --> 00:13:21,598
Yeah. No.

218
00:13:22,435 --> 00:13:23,903
Fish, I know in
your own sick way,

219
00:13:24,070 --> 00:13:26,801
you love this city, and
Gotham is bleeding to death.

220
00:13:26,973 --> 00:13:28,737
We need this dirtbag to fix it.

221
00:13:28,908 --> 00:13:31,139
Enough talking. Hand him over.

222
00:13:31,477 --> 00:13:32,843
He has it.

223
00:13:33,746 --> 00:13:35,647
It's in his eyes.

224
00:13:35,815 --> 00:13:38,444
He has the virus.

225
00:13:39,085 --> 00:13:40,314
Really?

226
00:13:42,455 --> 00:13:46,256
So, tell me, James,
what's it feel like?

227
00:13:47,427 --> 00:13:51,523
Like it's taking all my
will power not to kill you.

228
00:13:52,932 --> 00:13:57,336
My! Harvey, when you say
Hugo here can save the city,

229
00:13:57,503 --> 00:14:01,065
does that mean there's
a cure for this virus?

230
00:14:01,274 --> 00:14:03,209
Fish, I swear to God
if you don't step back,

231
00:14:03,376 --> 00:14:06,938
I will shoot you and these two
nimrods right here, right now!

232
00:14:07,280 --> 00:14:09,146
Hugo, is it true?

233
00:14:09,682 --> 00:14:12,811
That you're the only one
that can stop this madness?

234
00:14:14,053 --> 00:14:16,545
Mmm-hmm.

235
00:14:17,090 --> 00:14:19,150
Obviously, I can't
give him up now.

236
00:14:19,359 --> 00:14:21,225
Fine. You've had your chance.

237
00:14:29,369 --> 00:14:32,601
Did you really think that I
would come without backup?

238
00:14:33,873 --> 00:14:35,034
<i>You're a killer.</i>

239
00:14:35,341 --> 00:14:37,742
Jim, dial it down, buddy.

240
00:14:37,944 --> 00:14:41,904
Victor, looks like our little
Detective Gordon is overheating.

241
00:14:42,315 --> 00:14:45,149
Perhaps, you should
cool him off. Both of them.

242
00:14:59,332 --> 00:15:00,595
Marvelous.

243
00:15:00,967 --> 00:15:02,833
Just marvelous.

244
00:15:06,639 --> 00:15:10,098
There he is, the
real James Gordon.

245
00:15:12,779 --> 00:15:15,408
Nice to meet you at last.

246
00:15:28,961 --> 00:15:32,363
There we go, Master Bruce.
Two lumps just how you like it.

247
00:15:33,232 --> 00:15:34,860
You hungry, mate?

248
00:15:35,768 --> 00:15:37,634
Can I whip you up a sandwich?

249
00:15:40,072 --> 00:15:41,563
Anyway, if all goes well,

250
00:15:41,741 --> 00:15:44,506
we should be able to head
back to Wayne Manor tomorrow.

251
00:15:45,344 --> 00:15:48,212
Although I was thinking
that we could go abroad.

252
00:15:48,381 --> 00:15:50,179
We could go to Switzerland.

253
00:15:50,917 --> 00:15:53,195
I mean, we used to go with your
mum and dad this time of year...

254
00:15:53,219 --> 00:15:54,414
Stop it.

255
00:15:55,855 --> 00:15:57,847
Your attempts to elicit
an emotional response

256
00:15:58,024 --> 00:16:01,586
by reminding me of shared
memories is clumsy and pathetic.

257
00:16:01,761 --> 00:16:02,761
Oh.

258
00:16:04,530 --> 00:16:07,193
The last memory I have is
of you killing the best friend

259
00:16:07,366 --> 00:16:08,732
and teacher I ever had.

260
00:16:10,369 --> 00:16:13,100
You mean that old
geezer that kidnapped you,

261
00:16:13,272 --> 00:16:17,004
poisoned your mind, and tried
to turn you into a mass murderer?

262
00:16:17,376 --> 00:16:23,043
Let me tell you something,
Master Bruce, that man lied to you.

263
00:16:24,016 --> 00:16:26,144
Him and his bloody
Court of Owls,

264
00:16:26,319 --> 00:16:28,845
they tried to use you, they
tried to manipulate you.

265
00:16:29,021 --> 00:16:30,546
You say he was a liar.

266
00:16:32,758 --> 00:16:33,782
How?

267
00:16:34,994 --> 00:16:36,834
By taking away the pain
I've carried for years?

268
00:16:36,996 --> 00:16:39,932
By giving me revenge against the
people who killed my mother and father?

269
00:16:43,135 --> 00:16:44,694
That's more than you ever did.

270
00:16:49,775 --> 00:16:52,108
Anyway, the Court of
Owls does not matter.

271
00:16:53,312 --> 00:16:56,646
They merely paved the way
for the one who is to come.

272
00:16:57,517 --> 00:16:59,042
What do you mean?

273
00:17:00,820 --> 00:17:02,516
Who... Who's coming?

274
00:17:06,826 --> 00:17:08,192
You'll see.

275
00:17:12,532 --> 00:17:14,524
- I should cook him.
- They want him alive.

276
00:17:15,034 --> 00:17:16,594
So I'll just cook part of him.

277
00:17:16,769 --> 00:17:20,069
No, my dear, let's be calm.

278
00:17:20,273 --> 00:17:21,866
You don't have
that kind of control.

279
00:17:22,074 --> 00:17:25,943
And you do? In my hands,
this flamethrower is a scalpel.

280
00:17:26,145 --> 00:17:28,273
Fine. We'll each take a foot.

281
00:17:29,482 --> 00:17:32,213
- Whoever goes above the ankle loses.
- You're on.

282
00:17:32,385 --> 00:17:36,948
Let me... No, no, no! Stop!
Miss Mooney! Miss Mooney!

283
00:17:37,123 --> 00:17:38,591
<i>Mooney's busy!</i>

284
00:17:40,393 --> 00:17:41,622
I'm here now.

285
00:17:46,332 --> 00:17:48,699
Also, I think your children
are angry with you.

286
00:17:49,001 --> 00:17:51,436
- Mr. Cobblepot.
- It's understandable.

287
00:17:52,572 --> 00:17:55,701
You made them what they are,

288
00:17:56,642 --> 00:17:58,042
then abandoned them.

289
00:17:58,344 --> 00:18:01,109
You are working
with Miss Mooney?

290
00:18:01,614 --> 00:18:03,082
We're partners.

291
00:18:03,382 --> 00:18:05,351
But you tried to kill her.

292
00:18:06,452 --> 00:18:08,148
And she forgave me.

293
00:18:08,521 --> 00:18:10,456
I know, surprised me, too.

294
00:18:10,623 --> 00:18:14,719
But Mooney, is not the old
Mooney. She has evolved.

295
00:18:15,328 --> 00:18:17,422
And she has a vision for Gotham.

296
00:18:18,497 --> 00:18:21,763
She sees a city where
people like myself,

297
00:18:22,368 --> 00:18:24,030
Victor, Bridgit,

298
00:18:25,037 --> 00:18:27,700
freaks, are in charge.

299
00:18:30,409 --> 00:18:32,605
And you are gonna
help us achieve that.

300
00:18:33,512 --> 00:18:36,346
- I can't.
- Wrong, Professor!

301
00:18:37,583 --> 00:18:40,712
This virus is tearing
Gotham apart!

302
00:18:41,320 --> 00:18:45,314
That makes your antidote the
most valuable thing in the city!

303
00:18:45,658 --> 00:18:48,253
We could demand half of Gotham

304
00:18:48,828 --> 00:18:51,457
and the city council would
deliver it to us on a platter.

305
00:18:51,664 --> 00:18:54,998
So, I'm going to ask you once,

306
00:18:56,102 --> 00:18:57,229
where is it?

307
00:18:58,137 --> 00:19:01,266
If I tell you where
the antidote is,

308
00:19:02,541 --> 00:19:03,839
I have nothing.

309
00:19:05,378 --> 00:19:06,676
I can't.

310
00:19:09,782 --> 00:19:11,808
You can torture me all you want.

311
00:19:15,187 --> 00:19:16,246
Okay.

312
00:19:16,455 --> 00:19:17,923
What?

313
00:19:18,124 --> 00:19:21,856
You know, when I was in
Arkham, I was tortured daily.

314
00:19:22,094 --> 00:19:24,825
No. Well, that was
therapy, Oswald.

315
00:19:25,698 --> 00:19:26,757
Therapy.

316
00:19:29,201 --> 00:19:32,899
And that device you used
to administer the therapy,

317
00:19:33,339 --> 00:19:34,830
remember that?

318
00:19:35,741 --> 00:19:39,837
It gave the sensation that
your head was being torn open

319
00:19:40,012 --> 00:19:43,608
so that hot lava could be
poured directly into your brain.

320
00:19:44,517 --> 00:19:48,887
Afterwards, just thinking of it
would make me physically ill.

321
00:19:53,426 --> 00:19:56,055
So, naturally, I had to have it!

322
00:20:01,567 --> 00:20:03,229
One moment, Oswald.

323
00:20:03,402 --> 00:20:05,166
- No!
- All right, all right!

324
00:20:05,337 --> 00:20:09,035
I'll tell you anything you need to
know. I'll tell you where the antidote is.

325
00:20:09,208 --> 00:20:10,403
I know.

326
00:20:11,377 --> 00:20:13,676
But not just yet, okay?

327
00:20:14,180 --> 00:20:15,409
Or what?

328
00:20:26,192 --> 00:20:28,712
They're not answering at the
precinct. They must be overwhelmed.

329
00:20:28,861 --> 00:20:30,796
Well, we're not
shooting our way out.

330
00:20:31,263 --> 00:20:32,390
<i>Killer.</i>

331
00:20:36,535 --> 00:20:38,470
Jim. Take it easy.
Someone will come!

332
00:20:38,637 --> 00:20:42,074
Yeah! And by then Mooney will have
gotten Strange to give her the antidote.

333
00:20:42,274 --> 00:20:43,572
We're running out of time!

334
00:20:47,947 --> 00:20:49,040
<i>Killer.</i>

335
00:20:49,949 --> 00:20:52,111
<i>Killer. Killer.</i>

336
00:20:53,586 --> 00:20:54,679
<i>Killer.</i>

337
00:21:09,735 --> 00:21:11,533
I knew you could do it.

338
00:21:16,408 --> 00:21:17,467
Jim!

339
00:21:18,878 --> 00:21:22,406
Fight the damn virus!
Not my car. That's my car.

340
00:21:25,985 --> 00:21:27,180
Let me drive.

341
00:21:28,187 --> 00:21:32,249
Alvarez, spread the word, Mayor
James has called in the National Guard.

342
00:21:32,558 --> 00:21:34,754
We don't want any soldiers
getting shot by mistake.

343
00:21:34,927 --> 00:21:36,327
Leave me alone.

344
00:21:36,529 --> 00:21:38,225
The hell's wrong with you?

345
00:21:39,098 --> 00:21:41,124
Alvarez. Talking to you.

346
00:21:41,600 --> 00:21:44,195
I said, leave me alone!

347
00:21:49,441 --> 00:21:52,809
So, I will ask you
again. Who's coming?

348
00:21:53,779 --> 00:21:56,544
I mean, I thought the man that I
dispatched at Wayne Enterprises

349
00:21:56,715 --> 00:21:58,183
was the leader of
the Court of Owls?

350
00:21:58,350 --> 00:21:59,477
I want you to leave.

351
00:21:59,652 --> 00:22:01,572
Yeah, well, that ain't
gonna happen, is it, mate?

352
00:22:01,720 --> 00:22:03,746
You can't rid of me that easy.

353
00:22:04,857 --> 00:22:08,123
You have to
remember who you are.

354
00:22:08,427 --> 00:22:12,091
I know who I am.
I have a destiny!

355
00:22:12,431 --> 00:22:13,922
Now, you listen to me.

356
00:22:15,267 --> 00:22:18,328
That man that wanted
you to detonate that bomb,

357
00:22:19,738 --> 00:22:24,369
whatever he promised you,
freedom from pain, power, none of it,

358
00:22:24,910 --> 00:22:28,608
none of it was real. I want
you to remember what is real.

359
00:22:28,781 --> 00:22:30,306
I know what's real!

360
00:22:30,482 --> 00:22:33,452
I got vengeance for my
parents' murder. That's real!

361
00:22:36,055 --> 00:22:37,114
No.

362
00:22:39,124 --> 00:22:40,558
No, that's not real.

363
00:22:43,829 --> 00:22:48,199
What's real is every time that
you were sick when you were a kid,

364
00:22:49,935 --> 00:22:53,770
your mum used to sit up with you all
night and read to you till you fell asleep.

365
00:22:53,939 --> 00:22:54,998
That's real.

366
00:22:56,075 --> 00:22:58,772
Or when you were seven and
you took your silly rowing boat out

367
00:22:58,944 --> 00:23:00,879
and you got lost in that storm

368
00:23:01,046 --> 00:23:04,813
and me and your dad were out
shouting and screaming, losing our minds,

369
00:23:04,984 --> 00:23:08,648
and when your dad
found you, how he cried.

370
00:23:11,390 --> 00:23:12,688
That's real.

371
00:23:14,026 --> 00:23:18,657
Yes, your parents died in
that alley three years ago,

372
00:23:18,831 --> 00:23:21,767
and maybe that man took
away the pain of that night,

373
00:23:22,434 --> 00:23:26,235
but there is no life, there
is no love, without pain.

374
00:23:28,274 --> 00:23:29,936
<i>He could not touch the love</i>

375
00:23:30,109 --> 00:23:32,738
<i>that your mum and dad gave
you, that you still have in you.</i>

376
00:23:32,912 --> 00:23:34,642
You still have in here.

377
00:23:38,250 --> 00:23:40,310
Same love that I have for you.

378
00:23:45,157 --> 00:23:47,183
I love you, Master Bruce.

379
00:23:49,194 --> 00:23:52,221
I would do anything for
you. I would die for you.

380
00:23:54,366 --> 00:23:57,165
You must find that love again.

381
00:24:02,174 --> 00:24:04,370
Come back to me, Master Bruce.

382
00:24:55,361 --> 00:24:57,592
- Thank you very much.
- No problem.

383
00:24:58,464 --> 00:24:59,762
Excuse me.

384
00:25:06,372 --> 00:25:07,772
Oh, bloody hell.

385
00:25:15,547 --> 00:25:18,381
What I'm saying is, if Penguin
and Fish have hooked up,

386
00:25:18,550 --> 00:25:20,815
things are gonna
get real bad, real fast.

387
00:25:21,020 --> 00:25:22,113
You wanna run?

388
00:25:22,287 --> 00:25:25,951
No. I'm saying maybe she takes
care of Barbara and Nygma for us.

389
00:25:26,125 --> 00:25:27,569
I mean, we could
even help things along.

390
00:25:27,593 --> 00:25:29,562
Send word to Fish about
where Babs is weak.

391
00:25:31,530 --> 00:25:32,793
This is our shot.

392
00:25:36,168 --> 00:25:37,636
I'm not ready.

393
00:25:40,873 --> 00:25:42,899
What the hell is she doing here?

394
00:25:55,454 --> 00:25:57,013
Well, this is a strange day.

395
00:25:59,758 --> 00:26:01,488
Never thought I'd
see you in here.

396
00:26:01,660 --> 00:26:04,186
I had some time to kill
while my ex sees the light.

397
00:26:04,363 --> 00:26:06,127
Figured I'd have a little fun.

398
00:26:07,466 --> 00:26:08,798
Where's Babs?

399
00:26:09,134 --> 00:26:11,729
- What do you want with her?
- None of your business, errand boy.

400
00:26:13,539 --> 00:26:15,132
I'm sorry, what did you call me?

401
00:26:15,607 --> 00:26:18,076
I'm sorry, you're
not an errand boy.

402
00:26:18,243 --> 00:26:20,109
You're more of a shoeshine boy.

403
00:26:20,279 --> 00:26:22,199
They should give you
a little stand in the front.

404
00:26:22,281 --> 00:26:23,881
Cute little hat. That's
more your speed.

405
00:26:24,049 --> 00:26:25,813
Right. Out.

406
00:26:28,420 --> 00:26:29,945
- Oh.
- Yeah.

407
00:26:42,301 --> 00:26:43,462
You've got the virus.

408
00:26:43,669 --> 00:26:45,189
Wow, you're not as
dumb as I've heard.

409
00:26:45,270 --> 00:26:47,899
Are there any other glaringly
obvious remarks you'd like to make?

410
00:26:48,073 --> 00:26:50,474
How about I cut your lungs
out and show them to you?

411
00:26:50,676 --> 00:26:53,703
Wow. That's incredibly
vivid. I'd like to see you try it.

412
00:26:54,746 --> 00:26:57,238
But I'm here for your
boss, the crazy blond.

413
00:26:57,516 --> 00:26:58,745
She's not my boss.

414
00:26:58,951 --> 00:27:02,615
Uh-huh. I may have a virus making
me freakishly strong and mildly insane,

415
00:27:03,021 --> 00:27:05,388
<i>but even I know that you
were a sidekick to your brother,</i>

416
00:27:05,557 --> 00:27:06,991
<i>and you're a
sidekick to Barbara.</i>

417
00:27:09,128 --> 00:27:10,858
So, can you send
her a message for me,

418
00:27:11,029 --> 00:27:12,190
would you?

419
00:27:12,898 --> 00:27:13,922
Your boss.

420
00:27:15,868 --> 00:27:19,430
Tell her next time I see her, I'm
gonna rip her head right off her body.

421
00:27:22,541 --> 00:27:23,736
Bye, now.

422
00:27:32,784 --> 00:27:34,116
What, you need help?

423
00:27:49,902 --> 00:27:52,895
<i>Go back inside.</i>

424
00:27:55,207 --> 00:27:56,334
<i>Gotham's curfew...</i>

425
00:27:56,575 --> 00:27:57,634
Got him.

426
00:27:57,809 --> 00:27:58,833
<i>Sundown.</i>

427
00:27:59,011 --> 00:28:01,879
<i>All individuals must
remain indoors.</i>

428
00:28:02,648 --> 00:28:05,584
<i>Any activity outdoors will be
considered criminal activity.</i>

429
00:28:09,288 --> 00:28:13,282
<i>Clear here! Let's go,
let's go! Let's move out.</i>

430
00:28:17,129 --> 00:28:19,257
He's following
directions or something.

431
00:28:19,464 --> 00:28:23,060
Gotta find out who's controlling
him. Who's brainwashed him.

432
00:28:23,669 --> 00:28:25,137
And then what?

433
00:28:26,939 --> 00:28:28,771
I'm gonna kill the bastard.

434
00:28:33,145 --> 00:28:34,841
You two wait here.

435
00:28:35,280 --> 00:28:36,440
Professor, if this is a trap,

436
00:28:36,481 --> 00:28:38,921
you will soon find yourself
hanging with the rest of the meat.

437
00:28:38,951 --> 00:28:40,180
It's no trap.

438
00:28:40,352 --> 00:28:43,652
I tested earlier versions of the
virus and the antidote on livestock.

439
00:28:43,822 --> 00:28:46,621
I made sure to set
aside a successful batch.

440
00:28:47,025 --> 00:28:49,119
This place gives me the creeps.

441
00:28:49,928 --> 00:28:51,294
I like it.

442
00:29:07,512 --> 00:29:08,673
It's concentrated.

443
00:29:09,681 --> 00:29:11,343
Once you dilute it,

444
00:29:11,516 --> 00:29:15,977
there is enough here to cure
every infected person in Gotham.

445
00:29:18,123 --> 00:29:19,147
Hmm.

446
00:29:23,462 --> 00:29:24,657
Oswald,

447
00:29:25,097 --> 00:29:28,932
you and I will rule
this city together.

448
00:29:29,167 --> 00:29:33,537
Yes. But first, I have to kill
Ed Nygma. He has to die.

449
00:29:33,805 --> 00:29:35,967
Oh, he will.

450
00:29:36,875 --> 00:29:40,437
And all those who
try to stand in our way.

451
00:29:46,251 --> 00:29:47,651
What's this?

452
00:29:53,258 --> 00:29:54,590
Who's there?

453
00:29:55,594 --> 00:29:56,994
Show yourself.

454
00:30:07,205 --> 00:30:08,503
Who are they?

455
00:30:08,674 --> 00:30:10,370
Don't look at me, I don't know.

456
00:30:11,943 --> 00:30:14,503
Really? That's all you've got?

457
00:30:18,116 --> 00:30:21,086
Hand over the antidote. Now.

458
00:30:37,169 --> 00:30:41,766
I want the Strike Force and all
available units there now! I'm on my way.

459
00:30:41,940 --> 00:30:44,660
Reports of an ice storm and fireball
in the East Side Slaughterhouse.

460
00:30:44,710 --> 00:30:47,270
- You think maybe...
- Just drive the damn car!

461
00:31:11,670 --> 00:31:13,332
Sweet mother of mercy.

462
00:31:41,133 --> 00:31:42,294
<i>Killer, killer.</i>

463
00:31:51,543 --> 00:31:53,978
You damn fool!

464
00:31:56,148 --> 00:31:57,309
Fish!

465
00:31:59,618 --> 00:32:00,677
Oswald...

466
00:32:03,488 --> 00:32:06,253
It's okay, it's okay, it's...
We can get you some help.

467
00:32:06,425 --> 00:32:07,950
No. No. No.

468
00:32:08,193 --> 00:32:11,960
I've done this enough
times to know I'm finished.

469
00:32:12,130 --> 00:32:14,793
No. Do not say that!
We will get you help.

470
00:32:14,966 --> 00:32:16,434
Listen to me!

471
00:32:20,372 --> 00:32:21,840
Listen to me.

472
00:32:23,408 --> 00:32:25,877
Make this city yours.

473
00:32:29,047 --> 00:32:31,744
Or you burn it to the ground.

474
00:33:01,947 --> 00:33:03,813
People call me a monster.

475
00:33:06,284 --> 00:33:09,948
You! Jim Gordon, you're the...

476
00:33:12,457 --> 00:33:15,052
You're right. I am a monster.

477
00:33:19,931 --> 00:33:20,990
<i>GCPD!</i>

478
00:33:21,266 --> 00:33:23,167
Arrest 'em. All of 'em!

479
00:33:25,136 --> 00:33:29,335
Strange, you better tell me that
you can make more of that antidote.

480
00:33:31,209 --> 00:33:32,939
Yes, yes.

481
00:33:33,578 --> 00:33:35,740
I just need one thing.

482
00:33:59,704 --> 00:34:00,899
How's it hanging?

483
00:34:07,579 --> 00:34:08,774
You sure about this?

484
00:34:08,980 --> 00:34:10,004
According to my sources,

485
00:34:10,181 --> 00:34:14,585
Fish Mooney and the GCPD are scrambling
to recover the antidote to this virus.

486
00:34:14,753 --> 00:34:17,222
But Fish is dead.

487
00:34:17,889 --> 00:34:20,654
And Hugo Strange, who
designed the antidote,

488
00:34:20,892 --> 00:34:23,157
is setting up a lab in the GCPD.

489
00:34:23,328 --> 00:34:26,162
But they are missing one
very, very important element.

490
00:34:29,901 --> 00:34:34,669
So, yes, I am sure that this bozo
is the key to controlling Gotham.

491
00:34:35,040 --> 00:34:36,770
Are you my saviors?

492
00:34:37,876 --> 00:34:39,640
Are you the ones to set me free?

493
00:34:40,412 --> 00:34:41,812
Not exactly.

494
00:34:44,382 --> 00:34:46,248
Let's make Gotham beg.

495
00:35:00,966 --> 00:35:03,959
<i>Seek out the Yuyan building.</i>

496
00:35:04,135 --> 00:35:06,934
<i>Find the demon's head.</i>

497
00:35:07,339 --> 00:35:09,706
<i>Fulfill your destiny.</i>

498
00:36:38,463 --> 00:36:41,433
Right. Find Bullock. Let
him know where we are.

499
00:36:41,966 --> 00:36:43,832
I'm gonna follow Bruce.

500
00:38:04,649 --> 00:38:06,641
<i>I wouldn't touch that, Bruce.</i>

501
00:38:09,521 --> 00:38:11,012
You know who I am?

502
00:38:11,189 --> 00:38:14,057
<i>Who do you think told the
Sensei to send you here?</i>

503
00:38:14,492 --> 00:38:15,824
He's dead.

504
00:38:16,961 --> 00:38:18,520
He was murdered.

505
00:38:19,397 --> 00:38:20,626
He died.

506
00:38:21,800 --> 00:38:23,826
But he completed his task.

507
00:38:24,369 --> 00:38:27,601
The Court of Owls is
destroyed, Gotham burns,

508
00:38:28,039 --> 00:38:30,270
and you are here.

509
00:38:30,775 --> 00:38:34,576
He told me to complete my
training. To find the demon's head.

510
00:38:34,913 --> 00:38:36,779
You already have, Bruce.

511
00:38:37,782 --> 00:38:39,546
I'm the one you seek.

512
00:38:40,151 --> 00:38:41,881
I'm the demon's head.

513
00:38:45,123 --> 00:38:47,149
I am Ra's al Ghul.

514
00:38:55,366 --> 00:38:57,198
Why have you come to me, Bruce?

515
00:38:57,368 --> 00:39:01,829
The Sensei told me to seek you out.
That you would complete my training.

516
00:39:02,407 --> 00:39:05,639
And did the Sensei tell
you who I am, what I seek?

517
00:39:06,411 --> 00:39:08,846
I know you're not a
part of the Court of Owls.

518
00:39:09,013 --> 00:39:11,949
That you only use them.
But I don't know why.

519
00:39:13,685 --> 00:39:17,520
Then know that I have been alive
more years than you can imagine.

520
00:39:17,755 --> 00:39:19,417
That I have seen and done things

521
00:39:19,624 --> 00:39:22,321
that would shake the core
of everything you believe.

522
00:39:23,061 --> 00:39:25,394
That I'm thought to be a demon.

523
00:39:27,332 --> 00:39:28,561
A saint.

524
00:39:29,667 --> 00:39:30,862
A ghost.

525
00:39:31,669 --> 00:39:35,367
But for all my
years, all my travels,

526
00:39:36,274 --> 00:39:39,073
there is one thing
that I have never found.

527
00:39:40,411 --> 00:39:41,811
A true heir.

528
00:39:42,847 --> 00:39:44,975
<i>But I need to know
if you're ready.</i>

529
00:39:45,550 --> 00:39:46,643
I am.

530
00:39:47,619 --> 00:39:48,780
The Sensei trained me.

531
00:39:50,388 --> 00:39:51,617
Are you?

532
00:39:52,323 --> 00:39:54,019
<i>He set you a task.</i>

533
00:39:54,859 --> 00:39:58,796
<i>He asked you to be the one that released
the virus that now envelops this city.</i>

534
00:39:59,163 --> 00:40:00,358
You failed.

535
00:40:00,732 --> 00:40:03,031
I would have, but...

536
00:40:03,935 --> 00:40:06,063
But Alfred, he...
He distracted me!

537
00:40:06,237 --> 00:40:07,432
I know.

538
00:40:09,874 --> 00:40:10,898
I know.

539
00:40:11,075 --> 00:40:15,342
And that's why I'm gonna give you
another chance to complete your journey.

540
00:40:24,389 --> 00:40:26,415
Oh, don't look so
surprised, Master Bruce.

541
00:40:26,858 --> 00:40:28,884
I told you, you couldn't
get rid of me that easy.

542
00:40:29,060 --> 00:40:31,620
I just got a bit sloppy.
Got a bit of ring rust.

543
00:40:32,030 --> 00:40:35,262
Let these little ninja
monkeys get one over on me.

544
00:40:37,235 --> 00:40:40,137
You all right, mate?
What are you come as?

545
00:40:48,379 --> 00:40:49,506
Enough.

546
00:40:54,052 --> 00:40:57,784
This man is your past, Bruce.

547
00:40:58,990 --> 00:41:00,982
Now, embrace your future.

548
00:41:08,132 --> 00:41:09,395
Kill him.

549
00:41:17,442 --> 00:41:18,671
Join me.

550
00:41:21,312 --> 00:41:23,406
<i>Fulfill your destiny.</i>

551
00:41:30,688 --> 00:41:35,626
He's wrong, Master Bruce.
There's no other way to put it.

552
00:41:35,827 --> 00:41:36,988
He's wrong.

553
00:41:37,161 --> 00:41:40,256
Your destiny is to
be Bruce Wayne.

554
00:41:42,266 --> 00:41:44,735
And one day you're
gonna remember that.

555
00:41:46,604 --> 00:41:49,369
And you're gonna remember
how much I love you.

556
00:41:52,543 --> 00:41:55,707
I remember the first time your
mum and dad brought you home.

557
00:41:55,913 --> 00:41:57,609
They were so exhausted.

558
00:41:58,116 --> 00:41:59,948
And they gave you to me.

559
00:42:00,885 --> 00:42:03,753
This tiny defenseless
little creature.

560
00:42:04,689 --> 00:42:07,989
And they said, "Look after
him." And I said, "Sure,"

561
00:42:08,159 --> 00:42:10,355
and I scooped you up in my arms,

562
00:42:10,728 --> 00:42:13,562
and I held you, and
you opened your eyes,

563
00:42:17,001 --> 00:42:18,765
and you looked at me.

564
00:42:21,639 --> 00:42:24,040
And at that moment, I decided

565
00:42:25,076 --> 00:42:28,342
that I would do anything
for you. Anything.

566
00:42:35,586 --> 00:42:40,081
So if this is what you need to
do, Master Bruce, you crack on.

567
00:42:44,228 --> 00:42:45,526
You do it.

568
00:43:06,984 --> 00:43:08,179
Join me.

569
00:43:11,322 --> 00:43:12,483
Join me.

570
00:43:23,901 --> 00:43:27,394
Alfred! Alfred! Alfred!

571
00:43:28,406 --> 00:43:30,272
Alfred! No!

572
00:43:34,445 --> 00:43:35,879
Alfred!

573
00:43:44,489 --> 00:43:47,254
<i>You've broken through
your conditioning.</i>

574
00:43:47,959 --> 00:43:49,860
Impressive.

575
00:43:50,761 --> 00:43:53,390
You don't control me anymore.

576
00:43:53,831 --> 00:43:56,266
I will never be your heir.

577
00:43:56,434 --> 00:43:57,925
<i>On the contrary,</i>

578
00:43:58,102 --> 00:44:01,470
your strength only confirms
what the prophecy has foretold.

579
00:44:01,973 --> 00:44:06,934
<i>An heir to serve as my
knight in the darkness.</i>

580
00:44:08,813 --> 00:44:12,375
I will never follow you!

581
00:44:13,885 --> 00:44:15,615
You made me kill Alfred.

582
00:44:15,820 --> 00:44:17,755
<i>Use the waters, Bruce.</i>

583
00:44:18,689 --> 00:44:21,523
Our time will come.

584
00:45:09,440 --> 00:45:10,464
Bruce.

585
00:45:10,641 --> 00:45:13,839
Alfred. Alfred. Alfred. Alfred.

586
00:45:23,120 --> 00:45:25,817
<i>A city-wide lockdown
continues to remain in effect,</i>

587
00:45:25,990 --> 00:45:29,392
<i>with Gotham officials urging
people to stay inside their homes.</i>

588
00:45:29,594 --> 00:45:33,861
<i>As thousands of infected
citizens continue their rampage...</i>

589
00:45:44,075 --> 00:45:46,909
Lee. Where are you?

590
00:45:49,013 --> 00:45:50,606
Why? You miss me?

591
00:45:51,649 --> 00:45:53,049
City's not safe.

592
00:45:53,818 --> 00:45:56,378
Mmm. Well, that's
why I'm packing a bag.

593
00:45:57,088 --> 00:45:58,556
<i>What are you talking about?</i>

594
00:45:58,923 --> 00:46:02,519
I'm leaving Gotham. And I
want you to come with me.

595
00:46:05,263 --> 00:46:07,198
I'll take your silence as a yes.

596
00:46:07,398 --> 00:46:11,130
Lee. You can't leave. There
are checkpoints all over the city.

597
00:46:11,869 --> 00:46:13,360
Who you trying to convince, Jim?

598
00:46:13,938 --> 00:46:17,102
I can hear it in your voice.
You want this as much as I do.

599
00:46:17,842 --> 00:46:20,607
<i>We can finally be
together. Without judgment,</i>

600
00:46:21,212 --> 00:46:23,340
or secrets or jealousy.

601
00:46:24,982 --> 00:46:27,042
<i>After everything
we've been through,</i>

602
00:46:27,551 --> 00:46:29,281
don't we deserve that?

603
00:46:37,528 --> 00:46:39,793
I am leaving on
the afternoon train,

604
00:46:40,598 --> 00:46:42,590
and I want you with me.

605
00:46:44,468 --> 00:46:45,959
But I want the real you.

606
00:46:47,772 --> 00:46:49,968
<i>So tell me you'll
stop fighting it.</i>

607
00:46:50,141 --> 00:46:53,009
<i>Tell me I won't lose you again.</i>

608
00:46:54,378 --> 00:46:55,812
Tell me you'll be there.

609
00:47:00,518 --> 00:47:01,781
I'll be there.

610
00:47:05,656 --> 00:47:06,919
<i>Hey, Jim.</i>

611
00:47:08,225 --> 00:47:09,318
Where are we with Tetch?

612
00:47:09,527 --> 00:47:11,928
Barbara and Nygma gave the
Mayor's office a list of demands.

613
00:47:12,129 --> 00:47:13,188
Friend snuck me a copy.

614
00:47:13,364 --> 00:47:16,244
They also threatened to kill Tetch
if we tried to take him back by force.

615
00:47:16,534 --> 00:47:18,054
Half of these would
bankrupt the city.

616
00:47:18,169 --> 00:47:20,400
The alternative being
there's no city left to bankrupt.

617
00:47:20,638 --> 00:47:23,369
We don't have any cards to
play, partner. We got no moves.

618
00:47:25,176 --> 00:47:26,269
<i>Yes, we do.</i>

619
00:47:27,345 --> 00:47:29,007
- Him.
- Penguin?

620
00:47:29,213 --> 00:47:31,614
This entire list is
Barbara's except for him.

621
00:47:31,816 --> 00:47:33,536
Penguin is the only
thing Nygma cares about.

622
00:47:33,651 --> 00:47:35,244
- The question is, how much?
- No way.

623
00:47:35,519 --> 00:47:37,559
- There is no way we're turning him over.
- Why not?

624
00:47:37,688 --> 00:47:38,865
Because we don't
have the authority

625
00:47:38,889 --> 00:47:41,101
to broker some kind of secret
deal behind the city's back.

626
00:47:41,125 --> 00:47:44,254
Much less one that leads to the
imminent death of its former mayor.

627
00:47:44,428 --> 00:47:47,921
Nygma would betray Barbara and
hand over Tetch if given half the chance.

628
00:47:48,099 --> 00:47:49,692
I need to save Lee.

629
00:47:57,875 --> 00:48:01,539
I don't have much time,
Harvey. It's now or never.

630
00:48:04,014 --> 00:48:07,109
You know, one of these
days, I'm gonna say, "Never."

631
00:48:24,268 --> 00:48:25,429
- Hello.
<i>- Nygma.</i>

632
00:48:25,836 --> 00:48:28,772
<i>It's Gordon. I'm calling with
a proposition. Can you talk?</i>

633
00:48:34,378 --> 00:48:35,869
I can listen.

634
00:48:37,214 --> 00:48:39,206
We need to kill her.

635
00:48:39,417 --> 00:48:41,511
How much longer
are we gonna wait?

636
00:48:41,986 --> 00:48:45,150
Come on. Nygma
chopped off your hand.

637
00:48:46,056 --> 00:48:47,056
He almost killed me.

638
00:48:47,224 --> 00:48:48,715
And now, Barbara's
partners with him?

639
00:48:48,993 --> 00:48:50,393
That's the mother
of all insults.

640
00:48:50,694 --> 00:48:53,425
The city is gonna pay us a
lot of money to get Tetch back.

641
00:48:53,864 --> 00:48:56,129
We need to let that play out
before we do anything rash.

642
00:48:56,534 --> 00:48:57,763
I know you two were close.

643
00:48:58,803 --> 00:49:00,169
But whatever you had,

644
00:49:00,771 --> 00:49:02,603
she treats you like dirt now.

645
00:49:03,407 --> 00:49:05,467
She treats us both
like dirt and you know it.

646
00:49:06,977 --> 00:49:09,003
She doesn't
deserve your loyalty.

647
00:49:09,313 --> 00:49:11,009
What are you two
whispering about?

648
00:49:11,348 --> 00:49:12,907
- Nothing.
- Mmm.

649
00:49:13,184 --> 00:49:14,243
Any word from City Hall?

650
00:49:14,418 --> 00:49:16,546
Trust me. We're
about to own this town.

651
00:49:17,021 --> 00:49:18,785
Parts of it, quite literally.

652
00:49:21,926 --> 00:49:22,926
Where is Ed?

653
00:49:24,962 --> 00:49:26,430
He was just here a minute ago.

654
00:49:29,033 --> 00:49:30,695
Tetch?

655
00:49:34,305 --> 00:49:36,001
Nygma!

656
00:49:37,408 --> 00:49:39,168
- How could you let this happen?
- Us?

657
00:49:39,276 --> 00:49:40,556
You're the one that trusted him.

658
00:49:40,744 --> 00:49:43,009
I asked you to do one thing.

659
00:49:43,214 --> 00:49:47,777
Watch a man tied to a chair!
You idiots can't even do that.

660
00:49:53,390 --> 00:49:54,768
Where are we going? - Shut up!

661
00:49:54,792 --> 00:49:56,169
Look, I'm not trying
to aggravate you.

662
00:49:56,193 --> 00:49:58,972
It's just, this doesn't exactly have
an above-the-board feeling about it.

663
00:49:58,996 --> 00:50:01,074
- What's going on?
- Barbara and Nygma have Tetch.

664
00:50:01,098 --> 00:50:03,818
- They're ransoming the city.
- So what does that have to do with me?

665
00:50:05,135 --> 00:50:08,162
You're handing me over to him. You
can't. You can't. You cannot do this!

666
00:50:08,639 --> 00:50:10,835
It's a small price to
pay for saving the city.

667
00:50:11,008 --> 00:50:13,170
Yeah. For you. For me,
it's a very large price!

668
00:50:13,444 --> 00:50:15,310
Look, he cannot be trusted.

669
00:50:15,479 --> 00:50:17,914
You're risking everything
based on the word of a sociopath!

670
00:50:18,082 --> 00:50:19,607
Yeah, yeah. Get in the car.

671
00:50:21,051 --> 00:50:22,212
What? It's gonna be fine.

672
00:50:22,386 --> 00:50:24,412
Yeah. Penguin, Nygma,
Tetch, all in the same place

673
00:50:24,588 --> 00:50:25,828
for a high-stakes hostage swap?

674
00:50:25,956 --> 00:50:27,754
What could possibly go wrong?

675
00:50:39,003 --> 00:50:40,062
Do you mind?

676
00:50:40,237 --> 00:50:42,197
Look, if I'm gonna be
the city's sacrificial lamb,

677
00:50:42,339 --> 00:50:45,173
the least you can do is lead me
to the slaughter with a little dignity.

678
00:50:45,376 --> 00:50:46,400
No.

679
00:50:47,545 --> 00:50:50,709
You don't think that I can cause
you trouble once we're inside?

680
00:50:50,881 --> 00:50:52,042
You do and I'll kill you.

681
00:50:52,249 --> 00:50:54,616
No. You won't. Not
before you have Tetch.

682
00:50:54,885 --> 00:50:56,877
Not before the
exchange goes smoothly.

683
00:50:57,121 --> 00:50:58,765
And after that, what do
you care what happens?

684
00:50:58,789 --> 00:51:00,417
Let's just get this over with.

685
00:51:02,259 --> 00:51:03,488
- Thank you.
- Shut up.

686
00:51:10,367 --> 00:51:12,802
My three favorite men.

687
00:51:14,872 --> 00:51:16,465
Don't feel bad, Oswald.

688
00:51:17,007 --> 00:51:21,536
Your death at my
hands was inevitable.

689
00:51:23,314 --> 00:51:25,354
Is that what you told
yourself last time?

690
00:51:26,283 --> 00:51:28,946
I'm assuming the grenade's
not a fashion statement.

691
00:51:31,555 --> 00:51:32,579
Precaution.

692
00:51:33,290 --> 00:51:36,192
You three try
anything, I pull the pin...

693
00:51:36,860 --> 00:51:41,628
Kaboom! No more Tetch.
No hope for an antidote.

694
00:51:43,467 --> 00:51:44,945
Little crude, don't you think?

695
00:51:44,969 --> 00:51:46,835
Enough! Let's get this done.

696
00:51:47,037 --> 00:51:51,304
You're infected! How wonderful.

697
00:51:54,011 --> 00:51:56,105
<i>Nygma!</i>

698
00:51:58,749 --> 00:52:01,480
Did you really think you
could get away with this?

699
00:52:03,253 --> 00:52:05,065
I knew you'd figure out
that this was about Oswald,

700
00:52:05,089 --> 00:52:06,399
but how'd you figure
out where we are?

701
00:52:06,423 --> 00:52:08,756
Please. You know how
many cops I got on the payroll?

702
00:52:09,460 --> 00:52:11,656
Oh, baby, you might
wanna use your inside growl

703
00:52:11,829 --> 00:52:14,458
whilst making secret
calls inside the GCPD.

704
00:52:16,166 --> 00:52:17,566
Now, hand him over.

705
00:52:26,710 --> 00:52:28,042
Go!

706
00:52:38,522 --> 00:52:42,789
Let him go! Let him go!
We need to get Tetch!

707
00:52:51,368 --> 00:52:52,529
Now.

708
00:53:02,913 --> 00:53:04,381
That little bastard.

709
00:53:05,315 --> 00:53:08,149
Coming through. Move
out of the way. Rita, move.

710
00:53:12,456 --> 00:53:13,981
All right, let's have a look.

711
00:53:14,191 --> 00:53:16,626
Whoa. What did you
do to cauterize this?

712
00:53:17,194 --> 00:53:19,493
I don't know. Is he
going to be okay?

713
00:53:19,697 --> 00:53:22,929
We'll do everything we can. What's
your relationship to the patient?

714
00:53:23,367 --> 00:53:24,733
Doctor, BP's falling.

715
00:53:27,037 --> 00:53:28,198
We're family.

716
00:53:28,572 --> 00:53:31,292
All right. Let's get him typed,
cross-set and prepped for OR.

717
00:53:36,113 --> 00:53:39,049
It looks pretty good.
I'll call the station!

718
00:53:43,353 --> 00:53:44,616
Grab Tetch!

719
00:53:54,331 --> 00:53:55,594
Split up.

720
00:54:03,140 --> 00:54:04,164
Jim.

721
00:54:06,076 --> 00:54:07,772
<i>Jim.</i>

722
00:54:09,113 --> 00:54:11,673
<i>You and the ex
are infected, huh?</i>

723
00:54:12,716 --> 00:54:17,711
<i>I heard Lee wants to remove
my pretty little head from my body.</i>

724
00:54:18,956 --> 00:54:21,425
Is it weird that kinda
makes me like her?

725
00:54:22,025 --> 00:54:24,824
You thinking about ripping
anyone's head off, Jim?

726
00:54:25,963 --> 00:54:27,591
I bet you are.

727
00:54:28,398 --> 00:54:29,730
You're so close.

728
00:54:30,300 --> 00:54:32,599
The next time you give
in, the virus will have you.

729
00:54:32,803 --> 00:54:33,803
Stop talking!

730
00:54:34,004 --> 00:54:35,165
Jim!

731
00:54:36,774 --> 00:54:39,073
Come out, come out,
wherever you are...

732
00:54:39,243 --> 00:54:43,203
Hey. There's no back door. No
loading dock. No way this ends well.

733
00:54:43,614 --> 00:54:45,742
The virus will give you
all the strength you need.

734
00:54:46,283 --> 00:54:49,583
It's the only option.
Give in to the darkness.

735
00:54:49,787 --> 00:54:50,948
I said...

736
00:54:51,188 --> 00:54:52,188
<i>Killer.</i>

737
00:54:52,389 --> 00:54:53,914
Stop talking.

738
00:54:54,091 --> 00:54:55,616
You want to kill
me, that I can see,

739
00:54:55,893 --> 00:54:58,863
but without my blood
no antidote will there be!

740
00:54:59,029 --> 00:55:00,053
Fight it, Jim.

741
00:55:00,230 --> 00:55:01,562
I don't know if I can.

742
00:55:01,932 --> 00:55:04,128
He's right. We need him.

743
00:55:07,104 --> 00:55:09,630
Yeah. But not all of him.

744
00:55:14,511 --> 00:55:18,346
Where are they? What happened?

745
00:55:22,419 --> 00:55:23,580
What'd he do?

746
00:55:26,723 --> 00:55:29,887
Oh, Jim. You sick bastard.

747
00:55:30,928 --> 00:55:32,191
Where's the lab tech?

748
00:55:33,163 --> 00:55:35,962
Where's the lab tech? Come
on, come on. Here, here.

749
00:55:37,267 --> 00:55:39,930
What? You've never seen a
Mason jar filled with blood before?

750
00:55:40,170 --> 00:55:43,265
Go! Back to work!

751
00:55:44,208 --> 00:55:45,437
You okay?

752
00:56:01,291 --> 00:56:03,317
Oh! Oh!

753
00:56:03,694 --> 00:56:07,756
He's awake. I
was getting lonely.

754
00:56:08,098 --> 00:56:09,122
Where are we?

755
00:56:09,299 --> 00:56:13,327
We ran into a police blockade.
Had to hunker down a minute.

756
00:56:14,004 --> 00:56:15,529
Where are you taking me?

757
00:56:16,273 --> 00:56:19,835
I don't know. I'm sort
of improvising here.

758
00:56:20,277 --> 00:56:21,973
Why? You have
someplace you have to be?

759
00:56:22,279 --> 00:56:23,542
Does it matter?

760
00:56:24,314 --> 00:56:26,806
I imagine you're planning
on dragging this out.

761
00:56:27,150 --> 00:56:31,679
There are so few moments
of pure joy in one's life.

762
00:56:31,922 --> 00:56:34,858
I feel compelled
to savor this one.

763
00:56:35,325 --> 00:56:36,918
You mean gloat.

764
00:56:37,928 --> 00:56:39,260
Yes. I do.

765
00:56:39,630 --> 00:56:42,327
It was always one of your
least attractive qualities, Oswald.

766
00:56:43,934 --> 00:56:46,199
- It's killing you, isn't it?
- What?

767
00:56:46,536 --> 00:56:49,973
To know that you are not
as smart as you think you are.

768
00:56:51,241 --> 00:56:55,474
<i>All of that planning to drive me
crazy, strip me of everything I had.</i>

769
00:56:55,779 --> 00:56:59,978
Revealing yourself with a 'ta-da!'
and shooting me by the river.

770
00:57:01,718 --> 00:57:05,450
That plan was perfect,
and you know it.

771
00:57:06,590 --> 00:57:08,058
You failed.

772
00:57:09,159 --> 00:57:13,688
<i>I am still alive and you are
handcuffed in the backseat.</i>

773
00:57:14,231 --> 00:57:18,327
And now you will never be
able to correct your mistake.

774
00:57:21,071 --> 00:57:22,505
I guess not.

775
00:57:25,175 --> 00:57:27,553
<i>Now that they have Tetch's
blood, they can make the antidote,</i>

776
00:57:27,577 --> 00:57:30,256
<i>and after what we tried to pull, the
whole city's gonna be gunning for us.</i>

777
00:57:30,280 --> 00:57:32,592
Hell, I'm surprised the cops haven't
busted down our door already.

778
00:57:32,616 --> 00:57:34,551
Relax. They've got
better things to do.

779
00:57:35,619 --> 00:57:36,796
What are we supposed to do now?

780
00:57:36,820 --> 00:57:38,982
We split up, go to the
safe house and regroup.

781
00:57:39,289 --> 00:57:41,053
Regroup? For what?

782
00:57:41,224 --> 00:57:42,954
For whatever the
hell I tell you to do.

783
00:57:47,164 --> 00:57:48,928
I'm not waiting anymore.

784
00:57:49,833 --> 00:57:52,997
She's broken every promise
she's ever made to you. To us.

785
00:57:53,170 --> 00:57:54,570
I know.

786
00:57:55,105 --> 00:57:56,937
The safe house is the
perfect place to do it.

787
00:57:59,242 --> 00:58:00,505
Okay.

788
00:58:00,711 --> 00:58:02,009
I'll take care of everything.

789
00:58:02,346 --> 00:58:03,405
No.

790
00:58:04,948 --> 00:58:06,177
We do it together.

791
00:58:12,155 --> 00:58:13,384
Yeah.

792
00:58:26,136 --> 00:58:27,136
<i>Ooh.</i>

793
00:58:28,038 --> 00:58:29,870
Kowalski and Burrows
are gonna be pissed.

794
00:58:30,874 --> 00:58:32,206
<i>Tetch's blood is good.</i>

795
00:58:32,442 --> 00:58:34,843
The lab guys are starting work
on an antidote as we speak.

796
00:58:35,178 --> 00:58:37,841
I need to get to Lee. How
long? How long before it's ready?

797
00:58:38,015 --> 00:58:39,540
They said we could
head there now.

798
00:58:42,619 --> 00:58:43,712
Where is it?

799
00:58:44,021 --> 00:58:45,261
Detective Gordon, just in time.

800
00:58:45,455 --> 00:58:47,255
If you'll take a seat
and roll up your sleeve.

801
00:58:47,524 --> 00:58:50,404
<i>We have a dose ready for you right
now. The others will be ready shortly.</i>

802
00:58:51,461 --> 00:58:52,861
I need two.

803
00:58:53,130 --> 00:58:56,123
Sorry. We could only make one
of these single-shots so quickly.

804
00:58:56,299 --> 00:58:57,824
No. Two.

805
00:58:58,101 --> 00:59:00,101
All of Tetch's blood is in
the centrifuge machines.

806
00:59:00,203 --> 00:59:02,015
- The process can't be interrupted.
<i>- You're a killer.</i>

807
00:59:02,039 --> 00:59:06,101
Just one or two hours, max. You
can still catch Lee before she leaves.

808
00:59:06,476 --> 00:59:08,172
- There's not enough time.
- Ow!

809
00:59:08,378 --> 00:59:09,812
- Jim?
<i>- Killer.</i>

810
00:59:09,980 --> 00:59:11,004
<i>Jim?</i>

811
00:59:11,181 --> 00:59:16,085
Don't make me. Jim! No, Jim! Jim!
Damn it! Someone call the bullpen.

812
00:59:31,268 --> 00:59:32,497
Bruce.

813
00:59:33,870 --> 00:59:35,498
<i>I heard about Alfred.</i>

814
00:59:37,441 --> 00:59:38,966
Is he gonna be okay?

815
00:59:42,212 --> 00:59:43,680
Go home, Selina.

816
00:59:43,914 --> 00:59:45,314
What happened?

817
00:59:45,582 --> 00:59:46,582
No.

818
00:59:47,184 --> 00:59:49,016
- No. You don't get to do this.
- Do what?

819
00:59:49,186 --> 00:59:52,554
Walk back into my life. You
think I need your pity? I don't.

820
00:59:52,756 --> 00:59:55,749
- That's not why I'm here.
- You wanna know what happened?

821
00:59:59,763 --> 01:00:01,527
- You wouldn't understand.
<i>- Why?</i>

822
01:00:02,332 --> 01:00:04,597
Because I'm not desperate
to believe in something?

823
01:00:04,835 --> 01:00:07,703
Because you don't believe in
anyone or anything but yourself.

824
01:00:10,273 --> 01:00:11,832
It's called surviving.

825
01:00:12,809 --> 01:00:14,505
<i>And unlike you,</i>

826
01:00:15,378 --> 01:00:16,903
I know who I am.

827
01:00:18,014 --> 01:00:19,573
I don't need anyone to tell me.

828
01:00:21,151 --> 01:00:23,017
What are you even
doing here, Selina?

829
01:00:23,520 --> 01:00:26,922
You don't give a damn about Alfred,
and you sure as hell don't care about me.

830
01:00:29,659 --> 01:00:31,287
I know you better than that.

831
01:00:32,896 --> 01:00:33,896
Yeah.

832
01:00:35,565 --> 01:00:37,090
I thought you did.

833
01:00:40,971 --> 01:00:42,462
Have a nice life!

834
01:00:48,912 --> 01:00:50,073
Lee.

835
01:00:54,151 --> 01:00:56,120
I don't like to be kept waiting.

836
01:01:02,592 --> 01:01:03,753
You're still fighting it.

837
01:01:07,063 --> 01:01:09,123
I can help you with that.

838
01:01:11,902 --> 01:01:14,565
We both know
that's not what I want.

839
01:01:15,472 --> 01:01:17,805
I want you.

840
01:01:19,209 --> 01:01:22,008
I want you and
all your darkness.

841
01:01:23,180 --> 01:01:24,614
Give in.

842
01:01:26,816 --> 01:01:29,809
Give in to your
darkness. Be free.

843
01:02:01,017 --> 01:02:03,851
Don't you get tired of making
the same mistake over and over?

844
01:02:05,021 --> 01:02:06,455
You think I'm making a mistake?

845
01:02:06,656 --> 01:02:08,784
<i>Well, instead of killing me
when you had the chance,</i>

846
01:02:09,292 --> 01:02:12,057
you've decided to feed your ego.

847
01:02:12,462 --> 01:02:15,591
You wanna talk ego? "Riddler"?

848
01:02:16,566 --> 01:02:19,900
You will always fail, Oswald,

849
01:02:20,704 --> 01:02:24,300
because you will always let
your base emotions drive you.

850
01:02:25,542 --> 01:02:26,840
Hate...

851
01:02:27,210 --> 01:02:28,473
<i>Anger...</i>

852
01:02:28,845 --> 01:02:29,904
<i>Fear...</i>

853
01:02:31,281 --> 01:02:32,840
- Love.
- Shut up.

854
01:02:33,049 --> 01:02:35,161
You wanna know why I could
never love someone like you, Oswald?

855
01:02:35,185 --> 01:02:37,086
- I'm warning you.
<i>- Because you are a</i>

856
01:02:37,254 --> 01:02:41,954
spoiled child who throws a tantrum
any time he doesn't get what he wants.

857
01:02:43,360 --> 01:02:46,228
Especially when what he
wants doesn't want him back.

858
01:02:53,670 --> 01:02:57,129
You're right. I shouldn't
have waited. But unlike you,

859
01:02:57,307 --> 01:03:00,709
I am in the position
to rectify my mistake.

860
01:03:02,445 --> 01:03:05,813
Prepare for one massive tantrum.

861
01:03:17,294 --> 01:03:21,095
No! That is not possible!

862
01:03:21,498 --> 01:03:24,400
It is my turn! It is
my turn to kill you!

863
01:03:24,601 --> 01:03:26,467
Like I said.

864
01:03:27,404 --> 01:03:31,034
You will always fail.

865
01:03:31,975 --> 01:03:33,967
Because you'll never change.

866
01:03:35,078 --> 01:03:39,140
Maybe. But at least
I know who I am.

867
01:03:39,816 --> 01:03:41,751
<i>That day, by the
edge of the river,</i>

868
01:03:41,951 --> 01:03:44,580
that was the moment
you were reborn,

869
01:03:44,754 --> 01:03:47,724
and that was a lie.

870
01:03:48,325 --> 01:03:52,854
Your entire persona
is based on a lie!

871
01:03:53,229 --> 01:03:56,199
And there is nothing
you can do to change that.

872
01:04:00,003 --> 01:04:03,462
Actually, maybe there is.

873
01:04:10,013 --> 01:04:12,925
<i>Attention! All travelers must
pass through security checkpoints</i>

874
01:04:12,949 --> 01:04:14,508
<i>before boarding the trains.</i>

875
01:04:15,018 --> 01:04:18,614
<i>Please report anyone who might
be displaying signs of infection</i>

876
01:04:18,788 --> 01:04:21,155
<i>at the nearest checkpoint
or security officer...</i>

877
01:04:23,326 --> 01:04:25,090
Hey, this isn't a
public entrance.

878
01:04:25,995 --> 01:04:26,995
Oh, crap!

879
01:04:36,973 --> 01:04:43,573
Police! Excuse me! Police! Move aside!
Police! Move, move! Get out of my way!

880
01:04:44,047 --> 01:04:45,675
He's trying to stop us.

881
01:04:46,249 --> 01:04:48,184
You can't let him.

882
01:04:49,018 --> 01:04:50,611
I'll see you on the train.

883
01:04:50,820 --> 01:04:52,379
<i>Police, police! Move!</i>

884
01:04:52,589 --> 01:04:56,151
Out of the way, move! Jim! Jim!

885
01:04:59,896 --> 01:05:02,297
Now we're gonna be
delayed, aren't we?

886
01:05:02,565 --> 01:05:04,397
You gonna shoot me, Harvey?

887
01:05:05,802 --> 01:05:07,395
This isn't you!

888
01:05:07,837 --> 01:05:08,930
It is.

889
01:05:09,205 --> 01:05:11,003
Please, don't make me do this!

890
01:05:14,277 --> 01:05:16,075
Lee and I belong together.

891
01:05:17,280 --> 01:05:20,045
I know. I know how
bad you want that.

892
01:05:20,316 --> 01:05:23,548
To forget about everything that
happened, but you can't, it's not real!

893
01:05:29,592 --> 01:05:31,151
This is who I am!

894
01:05:33,963 --> 01:05:36,660
- This is who I've always been!
- No, it's not!

895
01:05:36,933 --> 01:05:41,667
Who you are is a choice.
It always has been, it still is!

896
01:05:43,873 --> 01:05:45,705
This is who you are.

897
01:05:47,277 --> 01:05:49,542
You're the best cop
I ever worked with.

898
01:05:51,014 --> 01:05:53,108
The best friend I've ever had.

899
01:05:54,384 --> 01:05:55,511
If you love Lee...

900
01:05:57,220 --> 01:05:58,518
Go save her.

901
01:06:07,697 --> 01:06:08,995
Tickets?

902
01:06:14,404 --> 01:06:15,736
Tickets?

903
01:06:20,276 --> 01:06:21,972
To our great adventure.

904
01:06:25,315 --> 01:06:26,647
<i>Tickets?</i>

905
01:06:59,048 --> 01:07:00,778
I love you, Lee.

906
01:07:10,760 --> 01:07:11,921
No!

907
01:07:16,065 --> 01:07:17,260
No!

908
01:07:18,334 --> 01:07:20,394
What have you done?

909
01:08:05,582 --> 01:08:08,177
<i>Really? A hacksaw?</i>

910
01:08:08,484 --> 01:08:11,113
<i>Even your disposal
tactics are idiotic.</i>

911
01:08:11,821 --> 01:08:13,289
Guess I'm just old fashioned.

912
01:08:14,257 --> 01:08:16,749
Did you really think I
wouldn't figure it out?

913
01:08:17,060 --> 01:08:20,724
The two of you have been
whispering like teenagers for weeks.

914
01:08:21,197 --> 01:08:24,759
Oh, Butchie. You
shouldn't have waited.

915
01:08:25,401 --> 01:08:30,635
Oh, believe me, if it weren't for Tabby,
you'd have been dead a long time ago.

916
01:08:30,873 --> 01:08:34,002
You're trying to tell me she
had nothing to do with this?

917
01:08:34,410 --> 01:08:36,106
- That's right.
<i>- Oh, so you've just</i>

918
01:08:36,279 --> 01:08:38,180
gone behind her back, have you?

919
01:08:38,815 --> 01:08:40,855
I was gonna hit you before
we got to the safe house.

920
01:08:41,217 --> 01:08:42,428
Play dumb when you didn't show.

921
01:08:42,452 --> 01:08:43,818
Leaning into your strengths.

922
01:08:44,287 --> 01:08:46,098
You want to know why you're
always taking shots at me?

923
01:08:46,122 --> 01:08:48,057
The giant size of the target?

924
01:08:49,425 --> 01:08:51,326
It's because for
all your tough talk,

925
01:08:52,762 --> 01:08:53,991
you miss her.

926
01:08:54,931 --> 01:08:57,264
<i>You miss her
loyalty. Her strength.</i>

927
01:08:57,600 --> 01:08:59,398
She made you
better and you know it.

928
01:09:00,236 --> 01:09:02,000
You sacrificed that, for what?

929
01:09:02,772 --> 01:09:04,400
To play queen for a day?

930
01:09:05,174 --> 01:09:06,335
<i>Pathetic.</i>

931
01:09:08,311 --> 01:09:12,146
If it helps? You never
deserved her in the first...

932
01:09:19,756 --> 01:09:21,588
I guess we'll see.

933
01:09:30,066 --> 01:09:31,830
I don't know if you can hear me.

934
01:09:35,071 --> 01:09:36,801
<i>But if you can,</i>

935
01:09:38,841 --> 01:09:40,571
Alfred, you need to fight.

936
01:09:43,379 --> 01:09:45,109
I don't know what I
would do without you.

937
01:09:47,583 --> 01:09:49,711
<i>Alfred, please.</i>

938
01:09:51,354 --> 01:09:53,323
Please don't leave me.

939
01:10:24,120 --> 01:10:26,487
Here we are. Again.

940
01:10:29,258 --> 01:10:30,351
Wow.

941
01:10:31,494 --> 01:10:33,053
<i>I have to tell you,</i>

942
01:10:35,665 --> 01:10:37,327
this feels really great.

943
01:10:38,768 --> 01:10:40,498
Glad I could help.

944
01:10:42,939 --> 01:10:44,498
Any last words?

945
01:10:46,609 --> 01:10:48,043
I'm fine for now.

946
01:10:49,912 --> 01:10:51,244
I beg your pardon?

947
01:10:52,248 --> 01:10:53,682
I'll wait.

948
01:10:54,383 --> 01:10:56,784
I'm going to kill you, Oswald.

949
01:10:57,086 --> 01:11:00,386
There is no later. If you
have something to say,

950
01:11:01,557 --> 01:11:03,253
now is the time!

951
01:11:03,726 --> 01:11:05,024
Duly noted.

952
01:11:06,329 --> 01:11:09,060
Whatever. I'm not
letting you ruin this for me.

953
01:11:09,232 --> 01:11:10,928
You don't have anything to say,

954
01:11:12,335 --> 01:11:13,928
but I do.

955
01:11:15,037 --> 01:11:17,404
Goodbye, Oswald.

956
01:11:29,685 --> 01:11:32,018
I removed the bullets
when you were knocked out.

957
01:11:33,122 --> 01:11:35,057
Right before I called them.

958
01:11:46,002 --> 01:11:47,766
In the backseat,

959
01:11:48,471 --> 01:11:50,372
the pin I used to
unlock my cuffs?

960
01:11:50,840 --> 01:11:54,004
My tie pin. I thought
it should be personal.

961
01:11:54,644 --> 01:11:57,443
You were just trying to make
me think I had the upper hand.

962
01:11:58,080 --> 01:11:59,810
It all fell into place.

963
01:12:00,383 --> 01:12:02,978
How did you know that Barbara
would show up at the warehouse?

964
01:12:03,853 --> 01:12:04,853
I didn't.

965
01:12:05,755 --> 01:12:07,314
If it wasn't for her...

966
01:12:07,623 --> 01:12:10,559
Gordon would have turned me
over, and I'd most likely be dead.

967
01:12:12,895 --> 01:12:15,126
But fortune favors the bold.

968
01:12:18,201 --> 01:12:20,727
You said you called them
after you knocked me out.

969
01:12:25,808 --> 01:12:27,436
You knew that
I'd bring you here.

970
01:12:29,312 --> 01:12:31,247
I know you, Ed.

971
01:12:32,949 --> 01:12:34,884
I may be driven by my emotions,

972
01:12:35,418 --> 01:12:39,116
but you are driven by
something much more predictable.

973
01:12:40,189 --> 01:12:45,253
A desperate, compulsive need to complete
what you've started in exacting fashion.

974
01:12:46,829 --> 01:12:48,593
Why don't you just
kill me, Oswald?

975
01:12:51,701 --> 01:12:54,102
You were the one time
I let love weaken me,

976
01:12:55,204 --> 01:12:58,197
and I want you around
as a constant reminder

977
01:12:58,474 --> 01:13:00,500
to never make
that mistake again.

978
01:13:10,353 --> 01:13:11,821
No!

979
01:13:24,433 --> 01:13:25,765
Barbara?

980
01:13:28,871 --> 01:13:30,066
Butch?

981
01:13:31,807 --> 01:13:33,036
Butch?

982
01:14:00,169 --> 01:14:05,073
Was killing Nygma really
that important to you?

983
01:14:09,011 --> 01:14:10,343
Did you kill Butch?

984
01:14:11,747 --> 01:14:15,445
He said you didn't have anything
to do with him trying to kill me.

985
01:14:17,286 --> 01:14:18,286
Is that true?

986
01:14:20,289 --> 01:14:21,621
What does it matter?

987
01:14:23,159 --> 01:14:25,060
All right, for argument's sake,

988
01:14:26,062 --> 01:14:30,158
<i>let's say I haven't
been the best friend.</i>

989
01:14:31,801 --> 01:14:35,499
Do you think we could put this
behind us and move forward?

990
01:14:38,908 --> 01:14:40,137
Did you kill Butch?

991
01:14:40,376 --> 01:14:42,140
That doesn't sound like a yes.

992
01:14:42,411 --> 01:14:43,435
<i>I need to know.</i>

993
01:14:44,413 --> 01:14:46,541
It's the only way we'll
be able to move forward.

994
01:14:50,152 --> 01:14:51,415
Yes.

995
01:14:52,755 --> 01:14:54,053
<i>I killed him.</i>

996
01:14:54,924 --> 01:14:57,291
But it's not like you
gave me a choice!

997
01:15:00,396 --> 01:15:01,659
There's always a choice!

998
01:15:54,550 --> 01:15:58,419
How many times have I told you
not to bring a whip to a gunfight?

999
01:16:13,669 --> 01:16:14,898
Now, we can move forward.

1000
01:16:22,078 --> 01:16:24,240
<i>The Tetch antidote has
been released over the city</i>

1001
01:16:24,413 --> 01:16:26,746
<i>with a 90% cure rate</i>

1002
01:16:26,949 --> 01:16:29,680
<i>with individual antidotes
now being manufactured</i>

1003
01:16:29,852 --> 01:16:32,048
<i>and given to GCPD officers...</i>

1004
01:16:32,922 --> 01:16:35,255
- You're awake!
- Ow! Ow!

1005
01:16:42,364 --> 01:16:44,060
I'm sorry, Alfred.

1006
01:16:46,135 --> 01:16:47,797
Wasn't your fault, was it?

1007
01:16:50,906 --> 01:16:52,738
I completely lost my way.

1008
01:16:54,243 --> 01:16:56,405
I've been trying to find
who I am for so long,

1009
01:16:56,579 --> 01:16:58,480
searching for some
greater meaning.

1010
01:17:00,616 --> 01:17:02,744
I don't know who I am, Alfred.

1011
01:17:05,421 --> 01:17:07,014
Who am I supposed to be?

1012
01:17:10,559 --> 01:17:12,323
I can't help you
with that one, mate.

1013
01:17:14,163 --> 01:17:15,893
You're a man now.

1014
01:17:17,766 --> 01:17:19,701
You gotta find your own path.

1015
01:17:21,804 --> 01:17:23,033
I'm not like you.

1016
01:17:24,607 --> 01:17:26,803
You've always been
so sure of who you are.

1017
01:17:27,109 --> 01:17:28,873
Oh, I don't know about that.

1018
01:17:30,212 --> 01:17:33,148
I've been through
some very dark places.

1019
01:17:33,616 --> 01:17:34,743
As have you.

1020
01:17:38,621 --> 01:17:40,920
You need to find your true north

1021
01:17:42,424 --> 01:17:43,756
and let that guide you.

1022
01:17:46,929 --> 01:17:48,158
What's yours?

1023
01:17:50,332 --> 01:17:51,493
You.

1024
01:17:55,070 --> 01:17:56,663
It's always been you.

1025
01:17:58,807 --> 01:18:01,572
You gotta find something
that you really care about,

1026
01:18:03,546 --> 01:18:05,845
and you protect it at all costs.

1027
01:18:07,816 --> 01:18:09,409
And when you find it...

1028
01:18:12,655 --> 01:18:14,146
You'll never be lost again.

1029
01:18:22,765 --> 01:18:25,792
<i>And though the arrival of the
antidote is certainly welcome news,</i>

1030
01:18:25,968 --> 01:18:28,767
<i>the death and the destruction
the virus left in its wake</i>

1031
01:18:28,938 --> 01:18:32,670
<i>will no doubt reverberate
through the city for years to come.</i>

1032
01:18:43,552 --> 01:18:44,679
Yeah?

1033
01:18:45,254 --> 01:18:46,449
Is Barbara around?

1034
01:18:47,990 --> 01:18:48,990
No.

1035
01:18:50,159 --> 01:18:51,650
And she's not coming back.

1036
01:18:52,928 --> 01:18:54,089
What do you want?

1037
01:18:55,364 --> 01:18:56,388
I'm not sure.

1038
01:18:57,499 --> 01:19:00,560
I just know I'm tired
of just surviving.

1039
01:19:02,338 --> 01:19:03,533
I want more.

1040
01:19:04,206 --> 01:19:05,640
I wanna move up.

1041
01:19:08,143 --> 01:19:09,941
Figured this was a
good place to start.

1042
01:19:13,616 --> 01:19:15,551
I'm at a bit of a
crossroads myself.

1043
01:19:17,620 --> 01:19:18,952
You hungry?

1044
01:19:20,556 --> 01:19:21,751
You buying?

1045
01:19:29,798 --> 01:19:30,993
Give it a whirl.

1046
01:19:56,091 --> 01:19:58,424
That is the logo
for my new club.

1047
01:19:59,428 --> 01:20:00,896
What are we going to call it?

1048
01:20:01,630 --> 01:20:03,531
The Iceberg Lounge.

1049
01:20:03,832 --> 01:20:05,892
Clever. 'Cause you're
nicknamed Penguin, right?

1050
01:20:06,602 --> 01:20:07,602
There's that.

1051
01:20:09,038 --> 01:20:10,336
And then,

1052
01:20:10,873 --> 01:20:14,867
there's the club's
centerpiece attraction.

1053
01:20:26,889 --> 01:20:27,889
Lee?

1054
01:20:29,725 --> 01:20:30,749
Lee?

1055
01:20:47,376 --> 01:20:51,746
<i>Jim, I knew if I saw you I might
not have the courage to leave.</i>

1056
01:20:52,881 --> 01:20:54,076
<i>And I need to.</i>

1057
01:20:55,317 --> 01:20:59,516
<i>I finally understand Gotham in a
way I suspect you always have.</i>

1058
01:21:00,823 --> 01:21:04,123
<i>It's a place where the
strongest and most cunning rule.</i>

1059
01:21:06,328 --> 01:21:09,821
<i>Where the cost of survival
is paid for by others.</i>

1060
01:21:12,768 --> 01:21:14,794
<i>And everyone feels alone.</i>

1061
01:21:17,106 --> 01:21:19,974
<i>Having the virus showed
me the city as it truly was.</i>

1062
01:21:20,943 --> 01:21:22,571
<i>As I truly was.</i>

1063
01:21:24,113 --> 01:21:25,411
<i>In so many ways,</i>

1064
01:21:26,115 --> 01:21:28,311
<i>the virus made me feel reborn.</i>

1065
01:21:28,484 --> 01:21:30,385
He's a gangster. Probably
got what he deserved.

1066
01:21:30,552 --> 01:21:32,646
- He is?
- Sure. That's Butch Gilzean.

1067
01:21:32,988 --> 01:21:36,891
Really? His chart lists his
birth name as Cyrus Gold.

1068
01:21:37,059 --> 01:21:38,059
<i>Cyrus Gold?</i>

1069
01:21:38,260 --> 01:21:40,559
Must have changed
it at some point.

1070
01:21:41,296 --> 01:21:42,540
<i>But if having the virus</i>

1071
01:21:42,564 --> 01:21:44,795
<i>allowed Gotham to
embrace its worst self...</i>

1072
01:21:46,001 --> 01:21:48,698
<i>The cure should remind
us there is always hope,</i>

1073
01:21:49,805 --> 01:21:54,334
<i>a chance to remember who we
can be, rather than who we are.</i>

1074
01:21:57,045 --> 01:22:00,709
<i>I don't know if Gotham deserves
saving, but I do know one thing.</i>

1075
01:22:01,683 --> 01:22:02,946
<i>If anyone can save it,</i>

1076
01:22:04,286 --> 01:22:05,618
<i>it's you.</i>

1077
01:22:06,889 --> 01:22:10,656
<i>And in return, I believe
it can save you as well.</i>

1078
01:22:12,828 --> 01:22:17,232
<i>And then maybe one day,
it will send you back to me.</i>

1079
01:22:19,568 --> 01:22:20,568
<i>Until then,</i>

1080
01:22:22,204 --> 01:22:23,570
<i>love always,</i>

1081
01:22:25,174 --> 01:22:26,403
<i>Lee.</i>

1082
01:22:41,390 --> 01:22:43,188
Can I come in, Captain?

1083
01:22:43,525 --> 01:22:44,525
No.

1084
01:22:45,928 --> 01:22:47,556
You threw me
against a train car.

1085
01:22:47,963 --> 01:22:48,987
I know.

1086
01:22:49,298 --> 01:22:52,462
Two, actually. I felt
like a freakin' cartoon!

1087
01:22:52,668 --> 01:22:54,637
I am really sorry about that.

1088
01:22:56,572 --> 01:22:57,767
You see Lee?

1089
01:22:59,708 --> 01:23:02,075
She's gone. She left Gotham.

1090
01:23:03,278 --> 01:23:04,439
You okay?

1091
01:23:06,582 --> 01:23:07,777
I will be.

1092
01:23:09,718 --> 01:23:10,913
You want to get a drink?

1093
01:23:11,153 --> 01:23:13,418
- It's noon.
- I didn't ask you what time it was,

1094
01:23:13,622 --> 01:23:15,386
I asked if you
wanted to get a drink.

1095
01:23:15,757 --> 01:23:17,248
Sure.

1096
01:23:17,893 --> 01:23:18,952
I'm good.

1097
01:23:19,895 --> 01:23:21,124
Any word on Tetch?

1098
01:23:21,430 --> 01:23:23,058
Yeah, he stumbled
into some hospital.

1099
01:23:23,265 --> 01:23:26,326
They patched him up,
shipped him back to Arkham.

1100
01:23:26,768 --> 01:23:29,237
You know, I'd actually like to
get back to being a detective.

1101
01:23:29,738 --> 01:23:31,366
Do some good,
old-fashioned police work.

1102
01:23:31,707 --> 01:23:34,700
The kind that doesn't involve
secret cults or blood viruses.

1103
01:23:34,943 --> 01:23:36,743
- Do we have anything like that?
- Not really.

1104
01:23:36,945 --> 01:23:40,177
Half the force is coming off
24-hour shifts, but we could, uh,

1105
01:23:40,782 --> 01:23:42,842
hit the streets like a
couple of beat cops.

1106
01:23:43,118 --> 01:23:45,144
See if we could stir
up some trouble?

1107
01:23:45,487 --> 01:23:48,150
I don't know. Seems
kinda beneath me.

1108
01:23:48,957 --> 01:23:53,258
You know, seeing as I'm the best
cop you've ever worked with and all.

1109
01:23:53,495 --> 01:23:55,855
I was just telling you
whatever crap came to mind

1110
01:23:55,898 --> 01:23:57,696
so you wouldn't punch
a hole through my head.

1111
01:23:57,933 --> 01:23:59,196
Like a hostage negotiation.

1112
01:23:59,368 --> 01:24:00,712
You just tell someone
what they want to hear.

1113
01:24:00,736 --> 01:24:01,829
Sure, sure.

1114
01:24:02,104 --> 01:24:04,596
- Now if you didn't have the virus...
- Is that right?

1115
01:24:11,747 --> 01:24:13,648
It was so good.

1116
01:24:19,688 --> 01:24:21,350
Money! Now!

1117
01:24:21,557 --> 01:24:23,150
- Dad?
- It's okay, sweetheart.

1118
01:24:23,325 --> 01:24:24,418
Now!

1119
01:24:27,629 --> 01:24:28,756
No!

1120
01:26:14,903 --> 01:26:15,903
English-SDH
